message: "If you use TED, cite the version-specific software archive and the method article when available."
title: "Trajectory Pathway Event Discovery (TED): an artifact-aware protocol for structured interpretation of dynamic pathway events in single-cell genomics"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-17
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21403133
authors:
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Kuanghao
  - family-names: Shi
    given-names: Hong
repository-code: "https://github.com/shayuanxukuang/pyfgsea-TED"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21403133"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - single-cell genomics
  - trajectory analysis
  - pathway analysis
  - event discovery
  - evidence provenance
  - reproducible bioinformatics
abstract: >-
  TED converts pathway, module or perturbation activity profiles into structured
  event objects that record event mode, artifact controls, identifiability,
  within-study support and external-evidence provenance. PyFgsea is an optional
  upstream activity generator; TED is a separate downstream inference task.
